  "notes": [
    "Weights are model education populations R(m,s,a,e), not survey sample sizes.",
    "TV is half the L1 distance between the variant and baseline P(income | area, sex, age, education).",
    "All variants keep the v1 income margins and the census education margins; they change only how the fixed margins are split.",
    "lambda variants temper only the paid-income initial shape q(y|s,a,e); education-specific employment rates stay unless the variant name says common_rate, so lambda_0.0 alone does not remove the education-income association from the final distribution that includes non-workers.",
    "This is a sensitivity analysis of transported assumptions, not a validation against observed municipal education x income data."
  ]
